{"title":"Career Roadmap · Geriatric Caregiver","role":"Geriatric Caregiver","summary":"A Geriatric Caregiver provides day-to-day supportive care for older adults who may need assistance with mobility, personal activities, nutrition, medication routines, companionship, safety and coordination with healthcare professionals.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Geriatric Care / Palliative Care Assistant"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Geriatric Caregiver provides day-to-day supportive care for older adults who may need assistance with mobility, personal activities, nutrition, medication routines, companionship, safety and coordination with healthcare professionals."},{"type":"p","text":"Caregivers may work in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Homes"},{"text":"Hospitals"},{"text":"Senior-care facilities"},{"text":"Assisted-living centres"},{"text":"Nursing homes"},{"text":"Rehabilitation centres"},{"text":"Palliative-care facilities"},{"text":"Community-care programs"},{"text":"Home-healthcare organizations"},{"text":"The role is particularly important as older adults increasingly require long-term, home-based and coordinated care."}]},{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Assistance with activities of daily living"},{"text":"Mobility support"},{"text":"Personal hygiene"},{"text":"Feeding assistance"},{"text":"Positioning"},{"text":"Fall prevention"},{"text":"Basic observation"},{"text":"Appointment coordination"},{"text":"Companionship"},{"text":"Emotional support"},{"text":"Care documentation"},{"text":"Family communication"},{"text":"Escalation of concerning symptoms"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Qualification note","text":"“Geriatric Caregiver” is a broad support-care occupation rather than a single uniformly regulated clinical profession. A caregiver should not be presented as a nurse, physiotherapist, doctor or independent medical practitioner unless separately qualified and authorized. Clinical procedures, medication decisions and medical assessments must remain within the caregiver's training and the responsible healthcare professional's instructions."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Class 12","Relevant Healthcare / Allied-Health Education","Geriatric Care Training","Clinical / Elder-Care Internship","Geriatric Caregiver","Senior Caregiver","Lead Caregiver / Care Coordinator","Geriatric Care Supervisor","Senior-Care Operations Manager"]},{"type":"h","text":"Home-care pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["Healthcare Qualification","Geriatric Care Training","Home Healthcare Internship","Home Caregiver","Senior Home Caregiver","Care Coordinator","Home Healthcare Supervisor"]}]},{"heading":"What You Learn During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Human & Healthcare Foundation"},{"type":"h","text":"Biomedical foundation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Anatomy"},{"text":"Physiology"},{"text":"Basic biochemistry"},{"text":"Microbiology"},{"text":"Nutrition"},{"text":"Psychology"},{"text":"Sociology"},{"text":"Basic pathology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare fundamentals"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"First aid"},{"text":"Basic life support"},{"text":"Infection prevention"},{"text":"Patient safety"},{"text":"Healthcare communication"},{"text":"Medical terminology"},{"text":"Ethics"},{"text":"Confidentiality"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Geriatric introduction"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Normal ageing"},{"text":"Physical changes with ageing"},{"text":"Psychological changes"},{"text":"Social changes"},{"text":"Functional decline"},{"text":"Independence and dignity"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Geriatric Health & Daily Care"},{"type":"p","text":"Students develop stronger knowledge of common needs among older adults."},{"type":"h","text":"Major areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Geriatric health"},{"text":"Nutrition"},{"text":"Mobility"},{"text":"Rehabilitation fundamentals"},{"text":"Mental health"},{"text":"Chronic disease awareness"},{"text":"Community health"},{"text":"Pharmacology awareness"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Common conditions"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand basic care considerations for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Arthritis"},{"text":"Diabetes"},{"text":"Hypertension"},{"text":"Heart disease"},{"text":"Stroke"},{"text":"Osteoporosis"},{"text":"Parkinson's disease"},{"text":"Dementia"},{"text":"Depression"},{"text":"Chronic respiratory disease"},{"text":"The caregiver's role is generally support and observation, not diagnosis or independent treatment."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Advanced Geriatric Care"},{"type":"h","text":"Activities of Daily Living"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop skills for supporting:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Bathing"},{"text":"Dressing"},{"text":"Grooming"},{"text":"Toileting"},{"text":"Eating"},{"text":"Mobility"},{"text":"Transfers"},{"text":"Positioning"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Instrumental Activities of Daily Living"},{"type":"p","text":"Where appropriate, support may include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Meal preparation"},{"text":"Shopping"},{"text":"Appointment coordination"},{"text":"Household organization"},{"text":"Transportation arrangements"},{"text":"Communication with family"}]}]},{"heading":"Final Year — Professional Elder-Care Practice","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The student should gain practical exposure to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Geriatric wards"},{"text":"Senior-care homes"},{"text":"Rehabilitation centres"},{"text":"Home healthcare"},{"text":"Palliative-care environments"},{"text":"Community healthcare"},{"text":"Assisted-living facilities"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced competencies"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fall prevention"},{"text":"Pressure-injury prevention"},{"text":"Mobility assistance"},{"text":"Dementia support"},{"text":"Nutrition support"},{"text":"Emotional support"},{"text":"End-of-life care awareness"},{"text":"Family communication"},{"text":"Care documentation"},{"text":"Emergency escalation"}]}]},{"heading":"Core Technical Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Skill Area","Key Competency"],"rows":[[{"text":"Geriatrics"},{"text":"Understanding ageing"}],[{"text":"Personal Care"},{"text":"ADL support"}],[{"text":"Mobility"},{"text":"Transfers & walking support"}],[{"text":"Safety"},{"text":"Fall prevention"}],[{"text":"Nutrition"},{"text":"Feeding & hydration support"}],[{"text":"Dementia"},{"text":"Cognitive-support strategies"}],[{"text":"Mental Health"},{"text":"Emotional support"}],[{"text":"Rehabilitation"},{"text":"Exercise/activity support within scope"}],[{"text":"Infection Control"},{"text":"Hygiene"}],[{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Recognizing changes"}],[{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Care records"}],[{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Patient & family communication"}],[{"text":"Digital"},{"text":"Care-management systems"}]]}]},{"heading":"Daily Geriatric Care Workflow","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Care Plan Review","Patient Check-In","Vital / General Observation","Personal Hygiene","Breakfast / Nutrition Support","Medication Routine Support*","Mobility / Activity","Appointments / Therapy","Lunch & Hydration","Rest / Social Activity","Evening Personal Care","Care Documentation","Family / Clinical Handover"]},{"type":"p","text":"*Medication assistance should follow the care plan, training and applicable rules. The caregiver should not independently prescribe, change doses or discontinue medication."}]},{"heading":"Activities of Daily Living","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"ADL support is central to geriatric caregiving."},{"type":"h","text":"Personal care"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Bathing"},{"text":"Oral hygiene"},{"text":"Grooming"},{"text":"Dressing"},{"text":"Toileting"},{"text":"Continence support"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Mobility"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Bed mobility"},{"text":"Sitting"},{"text":"Standing"},{"text":"Walking"},{"text":"Wheelchair support"},{"text":"Safe transfers"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Feeding"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Meal preparation/support"},{"text":"Feeding assistance"},{"text":"Hydration reminders"},{"text":"Monitoring for difficulty eating or drinking"}]}]},{"heading":"Fall Prevention","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Falls are a major safety concern for older adults."},{"type":"h","text":"Risk factors"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Poor balance"},{"text":"Weakness"},{"text":"Vision problems"},{"text":"Environmental hazards"},{"text":"Certain medications"},{"text":"Previous falls"},{"text":"Mobility limitations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Home safety workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Identify Risk","Check Environment","Remove Hazards","Improve Lighting","Use Appropriate Mobility Aid","Supervise High-Risk Activities","Document & Report"]},{"type":"h","text":"Environmental checks"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Loose rugs"},{"text":"Wet floors"},{"text":"Poor lighting"},{"text":"Clutter"},{"text":"Unsafe stairs"},{"text":"Bathroom hazards"},{"text":"Inappropriate footwear"}]}]},{"heading":"Dementia Care","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Geriatric caregivers frequently support people with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Alzheimer's disease"},{"text":"Other dementias"},{"text":"Cognitive impairment"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Calm communication"},{"text":"Routine building"},{"text":"Orientation support"},{"text":"Familiar environments"},{"text":"Behaviour observation"},{"text":"Safe mobility"},{"text":"Nutrition monitoring"},{"text":"Family communication"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Communication approach"},{"type":"flow","items":["Approach Calmly","Use Simple Language","Allow Time","Avoid Arguments","Reassure","Redirect When Necessary"]}]},{"heading":"Mental-Health Support","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Older adults may experience:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Loneliness"},{"text":"Depression"},{"text":"Anxiety"},{"text":"Grief"},{"text":"Social isolation"},{"text":"Cognitive decline"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A caregiver can provide:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Companionship"},{"text":"Active listening"},{"text":"Social engagement"},{"text":"Routine"},{"text":"Activity support"},{"text":"Communication with family"},{"text":"The caregiver should escalate concerning behavioural or emotional changes to the responsible healthcare professional."}]}]},{"heading":"Nutrition & Hydration","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Older adults may be at increased risk of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Poor appetite"},{"text":"Dehydration"},{"text":"Malnutrition"},{"text":"Swallowing difficulties"},{"text":"Weight loss"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Caregiver responsibilities"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Follow prescribed diet plans"},{"text":"Support meal preparation"},{"text":"Encourage appropriate hydration"},{"text":"Observe eating patterns"},{"text":"Record intake when required"},{"text":"Report significant changes"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For patients with swallowing disorders, caregivers should follow the recommendations of the appropriate clinical team rather than independently changing food texture or feeding plans."}]},{"heading":"Mobility & Transfer Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A caregiver should learn safe techniques for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Bed-to-chair transfer"},{"text":"Chair-to-bed transfer"},{"text":"Walking assistance"},{"text":"Wheelchair use"},{"text":"Repositioning"},{"text":"Use of walkers"},{"text":"Use of canes"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Transfer principle"},{"type":"flow","items":["Assess Patient Ability","Prepare Environment","Use Correct Technique / Equipment","Explain Procedure","Assist Transfer","Check Stability","Document / Report"]}]},{"heading":"Pressure-Injury Prevention","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Older adults with limited mobility can be at risk of pressure injuries."},{"type":"h","text":"Prevention"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Regular repositioning according to care plan"},{"text":"Skin observation"},{"text":"Clean and dry skin"},{"text":"Appropriate support surfaces"},{"text":"Nutrition and hydration support"},{"text":"Mobility encouragement where appropriate"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Observation"},{"type":"p","text":"Look for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Redness"},{"text":"Skin breakdown"},{"text":"Swelling"},{"text":"Pain"},{"text":"Changes in skin condition"},{"text":"Any concerning finding should be reported promptly."}]}]},{"heading":"Medication-Safety Awareness","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Caregivers may support medication routines depending on training and local rules."},{"type":"h","text":"Important principles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Correct patient"},{"text":"Correct medicine"},{"text":"Correct dose as prescribed"},{"text":"Correct time"},{"text":"Correct route"},{"text":"Documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Never independently"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Change dosage"},{"text":"Stop medication"},{"text":"Start medication"},{"text":"Substitute medicines"},{"text":"Interpret a new symptom as a medication indication"},{"text":"Medication-related concerns should be escalated to the responsible nurse, doctor or pharmacist."}]}]},{"heading":"Basic Observation & Escalation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A good caregiver needs to recognize changes in condition."},{"type":"h","text":"Observe"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Breathing"},{"text":"Consciousness"},{"text":"Mobility"},{"text":"Appetite"},{"text":"Hydration"},{"text":"Pain"},{"text":"Behaviour"},{"text":"Temperature where trained"},{"text":"Blood pressur